{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 7.45,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "Dear both: the trip did deviate, and a partial refund of SGD 7.45 is due to the rider.\n\nRIDER — the route. The platform's optimal route for this booking was 14.0 km, CTE southbound throughout (EV-TRIP-00107). The GPS polyline covering the actual drive is 17.57 km (EV-GPS-00107, trace_distance_km), an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5%. That passes both establishment tests in POL-RD-01 (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It does not reach either materiality gate (50% or 8.0 km), so this is an ordinary, not a material, deviation.\n\nOn the trace itself, two separate things must be said. It is impaired at the admissibility layer: EV-GPS-00107 carries weight 0.30 and fired the issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath outlier on the final Raffles Place approach implying impossible speeds). It is NOT impaired for policy under POL-RD-07: there is no gap over 90 s (max_gap_sec 0.0), no jump over 500 m, and the sampling interval is 10 s. The deviation may therefore be established on the trace, and it is; the pre-pass down-weighting speaks to confidence only.\n\nDRIVER — your defence. You took Newton and Kim Seng and say the CTE was jammed. No traffic advisory was issued for that evening: EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0). POL-RD-03 accordingly exonerates nothing, and 'cte very jam tonight boss' is a general assertion that traffic was bad, which POL-RD-08 says does not discharge your burden. There was no rider instruction to detour and no amended pickup or dropoff, so POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-05 excuse no part of the excess. No pooled baseline applies.\n\nOn the two escalation arguments you raised [cap at 0.30, and POL-RD-10(5)]: both are rejected. The excess is not carried by the 0.30 trace alone. You yourself admitted the route — 'cte very jam tonight boss' in EV-CHAT-00107 (weight 1.0), and 'I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it' in your statement, an admission against your own interest — so an artifact independent of the trace carries the deciding fact, and under POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is the MAXIMUM of the independent weights, not the minimum. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor, so POL-RD-10(1) does not fire. POL-RD-10(5) does not fire either: an assertion that cites no advisory is a burden matter under POL-RD-08, not a clause invoked against an absent artifact. The trip identifiers match, the timestamps agree, every charge line has a counterpart, and the refund is far below the escalation ceiling, so no other POL-RD-10 trigger applies.\n\nRefund (POL-RD-02). charged_total = 36.60. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177. refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45. The 1.35 multiplier was read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00107 (the only artifact that carries it) and is applied to the recomputed fare, so it is not refunded as such. The 7.45 is above the 0.50 de minimis and far below 90% of the charge, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND and the rider keeps the balance.\n\nNo POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral: the deviation is not material and the driver's trailing-90-day record is 1 flag against 619 trips, below both POL-RD-06 tests — his lifetime prior_deviation_flags of 2 is context only under POL-GEN-01. No POL-RD-09 correction: this trip carries no ERP gantries, no tolls and no surcharge, and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The GPS impairment does not reach policy level. Under POL-RD-07 a trace is impaired for policy purposes only on a gap over 90 seconds, a straight-line jump over 500 m, or a sustained sampling interval over 30 seconds. This trace has no gaps at all (gaps empty, max_gap_sec 0.0), samples every 10 seconds, and its worst outlier jump is 331.8 m - under the 500 m limb. The deviation may therefore be established on the trace, and the pre-pass down-weighting of EV-GPS-00107 operates under POL-GEN-02 alone, which is a different question.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-GPS-00107, whose weight_multiplier is 0.30, without naming the issue codes that fired (GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED). POL-GEN-02(1) requires an advocate citing a sub-1.0 artifact to disclose the impairment and name the issue codes in the same claim; the claim acknowledges 'the GPS impairment' but names no code, so it is discarded."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Escalation is not mandated on this record. The deciding facts are not carried by the 0.30 trace alone: the optimal distance the excess is measured against is carried by EV-TRIP-00107 at weight 1.0, and the route actually driven is independently admitted by the driver in EV-CHAT-00107 at weight 1.0. Under POL-GEN-02(2), where two or more independent artifacts carry the deciding fact the cap is the MAXIMUM of their weights rather than the minimum, so no POL-RD-10(1) confidence-floor trigger fires; and because the trace meets none of the POL-RD-07(a) to (c) limbs, POL-RD-10(3) does not fire either.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites EV-GPS-00107, whose weight_multiplier is 0.30, without naming the issue codes that fired (GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED). It refers to 'the 0.30 trace' but names no code, so it fails the disclosure requirement of POL-GEN-02(1)."
    }
  ]
}
